<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Balkans and Hungary</p><h1 class="st-title">Provisional Government of Albania</h1><p class="st-meta">1912 CE – 1914 CE · capital Vlorë</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">First government of independent Albania, proclaimed at Vlorë in 1912 while Balkan armies occupied most of the country.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-balkan-war">First Balkan War</a>, as Serbian, Montenegrin and Greek armies overran the Ottoman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balkans">Balkans</a>, Albanian delegates gathered in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vlore">Vlorë</a>. On 28 November 1912 they declared independence, raised <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/skanderbeg">Skanderbeg's</a> flag and formed a provisional government headed by the veteran Ottoman official <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ismail-qemali">Ismail Qemali</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luigj-gurakuqi">Luigj Gurakuqi</a> among its ministers.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The government controlled little beyond <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vlore">Vlorë</a> and its surroundings, lacking an army, money or international recognition, while <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/durres">Durrës</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shkoder">Shkodër</a> and much of the south were occupied or contested. It set up ministries, schools and a gendarmerie on paper. Its fate depended on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london-conference-of-1912-1913">Conference of Ambassadors</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a>, which recognised <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/albania">Albania</a> in 1913 but left <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kosovo">Kosovo</a> outside its borders.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>An <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/international-commission-of-control">International Commission of Control</a> took over administration in late 1913, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ismail-qemali">Ismail Qemali</a> resigned in January 1914 amid rivalry with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/essad-pasha-toptani">Essad Pasha</a>'s <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/republic-of-central-albania">Republic of Central Albania</a>. In March 1914 the Great Powers' chosen ruler, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-prince-of-albania">Wilhelm of Wied</a>, arrived to found the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/principality-of-albania">Principality of Albania</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/provisional-government-of-albania.jpg" alt="Provisional Government of Albania" width="320" height="156"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Qeveria_e_Ismail_Qemalit.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1912 CE – 1914 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Vlorë</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Ismail Qemali</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam, Orthodox and Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Albanian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/albania">Albania</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Vlora government, Albanian Provisional Government</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1913&amp;focus=provisional-government-of-albania" aria-label="Provisional Government of Albania on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5158 732 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Provisional Government of Albania lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5478 988L5709 970M5478 988L5475 960"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5709 970h0M5475 960h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5478 988h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5478 988h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Vlorë. <a href="/atlas?year=1913&amp;focus=provisional-government-of-albania">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
